From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MASTER2 constitutional refactor <master@openbsd.local>
Date: Thu, 05 Mar 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [MASTER2] wave 2: WebSocket, VAD, March 2026 free models, OpenBSD fixes, self_refactor collapse

FINDINGS from DeepSeek deep-analysis + own review:

CRITICAL BUG — lib/server.rb kill_port_users uses `lsof`:
  lsof is not installed on OpenBSD. Uses fstat(1) + sockstat(1) on BSD.
  The command silently produced empty output → port cleanup never ran.
  Fixed: OpenBSD-native fstat/sockstat path; Linux lsof as fallback.

UX BUG — cli.html used HTTP POST /chat + polling /poll:
  DeepSeek correctly identified this as the #1 latency source.
  The WebSocket endpoint at /ws was ALREADY implemented server-side but
  cli.html never used it. Replaced all HTTP chat/poll with WebSocket.
  Added VAD silence timer: 1200ms after last interim result → auto-send.
  Added WebSocket reconnect with exponential backoff.
  Added interrupt: user speech during assistant speech cancels TTS and
  retransmits.

FREE MODEL AUDIT — March 2026:
  Added 4 models now available on OpenRouter but missing from data/models.yml:
  - meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct:free (128k, Meta, strong coding)
  - google/gemini-2.5-flash-preview:free (1M ctx, Google, best free reasoning)  
  - nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1:free (131k, NVIDIA, strong RLHF)
  - qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b:free (131k, Alibaba, hybrid reasoning)
  Reordered free tier: gemini-2.5-flash-preview first (1M ctx, reasoning:true).
  MASTER2 now has 12 free fallbacks. Zero-cost operation is viable.

PRUNING — lib/self_refactor.rb:
  DeepSeek: "SelfRefactor and MultiRefactor are the same core idea."
  Confirmed: SelfRefactor.run is 68 lines duplicating MultiRefactor behavior.
  Collapsed to a 12-line thin wrapper. Behavior identical, surface halved.

PRUNING — Gemfile tty-box, tty-markdown:
  Already removed in wave 1. Confirmed no remaining require calls.

CONSISTENCY — data/models.yml council.yml cross-reference:
  council.yml references "deepseek/deepseek-r1:free" and "qwen/qwen3-coder:free"
  — both exist in models.yml. New free models added to council fallback comment.

